{"id": "fa-01", "question": "Who serves on the SRMIST Plagiarism Assessment Committee, and to which office does the committee submit its recommendations?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/academic_integrity/10-complete_plagiarism_intellectual_theft_s"], "required_values": ["Librarian", "Controller"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Four members: Dean (convener), a senior professor of the department other than the guide, a professor of another department, the Librarian; recommendations to the office of the Controller of Examinations."}
{"id": "fa-02", "question": "What is the minimum attendance percentage required per individual course to be eligible for end-semester examinations, what absences does the remaining buffer cover, and what is the maximum condonation percentage allowed in genuine cases?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/7.3-minimum_attendance", "srm/attendance/7.5-condonation_of_attendance"], "required_values": ["75%", "25%", "10%"], "forbidden_values": ["80%"], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] 75% per course; the 25% covers medical, on-duty, sports, emergencies etc.; condonation by HoD + senior faculty committee to Dean CET, at most 10%."}
{"id": "fa-03", "question": "Under the Code of Conduct for Students, who can file an appeal against a disciplinary decision, who hears the appeal, and which misconduct levels are eligible for appeal?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/7-appeal_process"], "required_values": ["Registrar", "5", "6"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Written appeal to the Registrar; Appellate Committee (VC, Registrar, Pro-VC) headed by the VC; Level 5 and Level 6 only; final and binding."}
{"id": "fa-04", "question": "Within how many days of result declaration must a student apply for review, revaluation, or retotaling, what mark difference triggers a third examiner during revaluation, and which examination types are excluded from this process?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/XX-grievances"], "required_values": ["7 days", "10%"], "forbidden_values": ["15 days"], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Within 7 days of results; >10% difference -> third examiner, average of the nearest two; not for practical, clinical or viva voce. 'seven days' in words needs a manual look."}
{"id": "fa-05", "question": "What are the official hostel mess timings for all four meals, and what are the designated silence hours inside the hostel?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/residence/mess", "srm/residence/16.0-general_discipline"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Breakfast 7-9 am, lunch 11.30 am-1.30 pm, tea 4.30-5.30 pm, dinner 7.30-9 pm; silence 10 pm-6 am (16.24). Times are written in many forms: graded by hand, citation scored."}
{"id": "fa-06", "question": "What is the annual scholarship portal application schedule (opening date, closing date, and provisional list date), and which degree programs are completely excluded from SRMIST scholarships?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/2-diversity_scholarship", "srm/scholarship_categories/XIII-sponsored_scholarships", "srm/scholarship/14-faculty_of_medicine_and_health_sciences"], "required_values": ["July", "NEET"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Opens 1 July, last date 10 July, committee by 20 July, recommendations by 25 July, provisional list by 1 August; not for NEET-based programmes, Pharm.D, Pharm.D (PB)."}
{"id": "fa-07", "question": "What are the eligibility requirements, tuition waiver percentage, and ongoing renewal conditions for the Alumni Scholarship?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/9-alumni_scholarship", "srm/scholarship_categories/IX-alumni_scholarship"], "required_values": ["25%", "15", "10"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Parent: UG >= 15 / PG >= 10 years, registered alumni; first living child; 25% tuition waiver; renewal: apply yearly, CGPA > 7, no arrears, no break/detention/disciplinary action, parent participates at least twice a year."}
{"id": "fa-08", "question": "How long does the University store evaluated answer scripts, and what is the deadline and channel for submitting a complaint about a question paper?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/XXI-storage_of_answer_scripts", "srm/examination/VIII-question_papers_for_the_end_semester_uni"], "required_values": ["one year", "three days"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[DIRECT LOOKUP] Scripts stored one year (two semesters); question-paper complaints through the Head of College/Department to the CoE within three days. Digits ('1 year', '3 days') need a manual look."}
{"id": "fa-09", "question": "A doctoral researcher at SRMIST has already published two journal articles based on her thesis work, one of which is co-authored with an external collaborator. She wants to include content from these published papers in her final thesis without being penalized for self-plagiarism (duplication). What exact steps and supporting documents are required?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/academic_integrity/3-duplication_self_plagiarism_reuse"], "required_values": ["certificate", "consent"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Cite her own articles; supervisor's certificate listing and attaching the published articles (only those excluded from the check); consent letter from co-author(s) AND publisher."}
{"id": "fa-10", "question": "A lateral-entry B.Tech student facing personal hardship wants to exit the program with a Diploma after the 6th semester and wants to take an approved 3-credit NPTEL MOOC instead of doing the 6th-semester Project Work. Is either part of this plan permitted under the 2021 Academic Regulations?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/1.5-admissions_under_lateral_entry_scheme", "srm/attendance/2.6-project_work", "srm/attendance/5.3-exit_option_and_award_of_diploma"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Neither: lateral-entry students exit only with a B.Tech/M.Tech (R 1.5); diploma-exit students must do the Project Work, no MOOC (R 2.6)."}
{"id": "fa-11", "question": "A 6th-semester B.Tech student with a CGPA of 9.2 wants to register for a Guided Study (Self-Learning) course this semester. Separately, in Week 3 of the semester, the same student decides to drop a compulsory core course they are struggling with. How do the Academic Regulations treat both requests?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/3.8-guided_study_self_learning", "srm/attendance/3.7-adding_and_dropping_courses"], "required_values": ["9.5"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Neither: guided study needs CGPA 9.5 (from semester VI, max two); add/drop is for electives only and within the first 2 weeks; a course dropped later is recorded Ab or I."}
{"id": "fa-12", "question": "A student caught misusing and tampering with their university ID card is given a 5-day academic suspension (Level 2 misconduct). Believing the penalty is harsh, the student submits a written appeal to the Registrar requesting a review by the Appellate Committee. Should the appeal be entertained?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/7-appeal_process", "srm/code_of_conduct/level_2"], "required_values": ["5", "6"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] No: appeals are permitted only for Level 5 and Level 6; ID-card misuse is Level 2."}
{"id": "fa-13", "question": "A B.Tech student fractures their dominant arm one week before exams and requests a scribe (amanuensis) for both a Theory exam and a Practical lab exam. They propose using their younger brother—who is in a lower grade and scored 52%—as the writer, and ask whether the University will pay the scribe. Which parts of this request are permitted, which are rejected, and what extra time applies?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/XIII-special_arrangements_for_amanuensis_scri"], "required_values": ["blood relative"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Theory yes (temporary disability), practical no scribe; brother rejected (blood relative), although 52% is under the 55% limit; the University does not pay the writer and a non-blind candidate pays an extra fee per paper; up to one hour extra time."}
{"id": "fa-14", "question": "A student arrives at the examination hall 35 minutes after the start of an end-semester exam due to heavy traffic, and also realizes they forgot their hall ticket back in their hostel room. Can they enter the exam hall, and what is the normal procedure for a forgotten versus a lost hall ticket?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/IX-conduct_of_theory_examinations", "srm/examination/XII-instructions_to_the_candidates_appearing"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] No entry after half an hour; forgotten ticket: duplicate from the Chief Superintendent for one session on paying a fine; lost ticket: CoE office, prescribed fee. '30 minutes' vs 'half an hour': graded by hand."}
{"id": "fa-15", "question": "In two separate incidents during end-semester exams: (a) Student A is caught committing malpractice during the practical component of a Joint (J-code) course, and (b) Student B is caught carrying a smartwatch into a theory exam hall for the first time. What exact punishments apply to Student A and Student B?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/annexure_ii"], "required_values": ["undertaking"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] A: the whole J-code subject, theory AND practical, cancelled. B: that subject cancelled + undertaking from BOTH student and parent; repeat -> termination. (Key corrected 2026-11-20: 'student and parent'.)"}
{"id": "fa-16", "question": "A 2nd-year hostel resident invites a day-scholar friend into their hostel room and takes them to eat dinner in the hostel mess. Later that same week, the resident's roommate fails to return to the hostel after 10:30 PM, and the resident chooses not to inform the warden. What rules have been violated and what penalties or liabilities apply?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/residence/mess", "srm/residence/16.0-general_discipline"], "required_values": ["2000"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Day scholar in room/mess: fine Rs 2000 (12.10); roommates must report anyone missing after 10 pm or are equally liable (16.33). 'Rs 2,000' with a comma needs a manual look."}
{"id": "fa-17", "question": "Two students request a prorated refund of their hostel room rent and mess fees mid-academic year: (a) a 2nd-year student who decides to move into an off-campus apartment, and (b) a final-year student leaving for a University-approved semester internship. What refund, if any, is each student eligible to receive?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/residence/7.2-all_other_students", "srm/residence/refund_of_hostel_fees"], "required_values": ["mess"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] (a) 2nd year moving out: no refund. (b) final-year approved internship: refund of mess fees only, case by case, Project Guide + HoD approval."}
{"id": "fa-18", "question": "An incoming 1st-year B.Tech student whose father is a serving paramilitary officer applies for the Defence Scholarship. Because their combined parental income is Rs. 4.5 Lakhs per year, they also ask to combine it with the Socio-Economic Need-Based Scholarship. Are they eligible for either scholarship, or both?", "category": "negation_exception", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/12-defence_scholarship", "srm/scholarship/4-socio_economic_scholarship", "srm/scholarship_categories/XIII-sponsored_scholarships"], "required_values": ["paramilitary", "II year"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[SCENARIO] Neither: paramilitary personnel are excluded from the Defence scholarship; need-based is for II year or above (income cap 6 lakhs met but irrelevant); and only ONE category anyway."}
{"id": "fa-19", "question": "A hostel resident finishes an academic semester with 80% attendance across all registered courses and passes every subject. Can this student sit for the end-semester examinations, and are they eligible to continue staying in the hostel for the subsequent semester?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/7.3-minimum_attendance", "srm/residence/16.0-general_discipline"], "required_values": ["75%", "95%"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP] Exams: yes (75% minimum; 80% is code 8). Hostel: no - below 95% attendance means no hostel stay for later semesters (16.17)."}
{"id": "fa-20", "question": "A hostel resident is found guilty of damaging campus property (Level 3 misconduct) and receives a 7-day academic suspension along with cost recovery. Beyond the suspension and repair cost, what other consequences apply regarding their parents, placement assistance, end-semester exams, and staying in the hostel during the suspension?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/level_3", "srm/residence/16.0-general_discipline"], "required_values": ["undertaking", "placement"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP] Parents in person + undertaking; 7 days suspension with tasks; cost recovered; disqualified from placement assistance and/or barred from end-semester exams; no hostel stay during suspension (Hostel Rules 16.17). (Key corrected 2026-11-20: cites 16.17, not R 3.6, which is about a break of studies.)"}
{"id": "fa-21", "question": "A B.Tech student misses one regular end-semester exam because of the sudden demise of their mother, clears that paper on the next available attempt, and graduates in 8 semesters with an 8.6 CGPA and no other failures or absences. How does this single excused absence affect their eligibility for (a) University Ranks/Medals, and (b) First Class with Distinction?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/II-a_procedure_for_ranks_and_medals_during", "srm/attendance/8.8-class_distinction"], "required_values": ["First Appearance"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP; AMBIGUOUS] Ranks/medals: still eligible - a parent's demise is an accepted reason, treated as first appearance. Distinction: R 8.8 requires no Ab/F/I in any semester; the policies do not say whether this absence leaves an Ab. ACCEPTED: an answer that states both rules and the uncertainty gets full marks. (Key corrected 2026-11-20: R 8.8, not R 8.10-8.11.)"}
{"id": "fa-22", "question": "A student holding an SRM Merit Scholarship attends only 70% of classes in one course, does not receive condonation, and therefore receives an `I` grade in that course, while still maintaining an overall CGPA of 9.1. What happens to their course registration for that exam, and can they renew their SRM Merit Scholarship for the next academic year?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/7.3-minimum_attendance", "srm/attendance/7.4-attendance_shortage_and_examination", "srm/scholarship/2-srm_merit_scholarship"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP; INTERPRETIVE] Below 75%: not allowed to write the exam, registration for the course cancelled, I grade, parents informed. Renewal requires no arrears/backlogs at the time of application; whether an uncleared I grade counts is an interpretation. ACCEPTED: stating both conditions."}
{"id": "fa-23", "question": "A hostel student is caught using an unauthorized hot plate in their hostel room and is fined, but fails to pay the hostel fine for 6 weeks. What consequences are triggered under the Hostel Rules, and how does the Code of Conduct classify unauthorized electrical appliances in a hostel room?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/residence/payment_of_fine", "srm/residence/16.0-general_discipline", "srm/code_of_conduct/level_1"], "required_values": ["vacate"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP] Hot plate forbidden (heavy penalty, repeat -> expulsion from hostel); a fine unpaid after one month -> vacate the hostel immediately; Code of Conduct: electrical appliances = Level 1 (parents informed 3 times and/or 3 days suspension)."}
{"id": "fa-24", "question": "If a scholarship-holding student is found guilty of severe plagiarism and recommended for rustication for a limited period, who takes the final disciplinary action, which governing bodies ratify it, and what happens to the student's active scholarship?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/academic_integrity/10-complete_plagiarism_intellectual_theft_s", "srm/scholarship/2-diversity_scholarship"], "required_values": ["Academic Council", "Management Council"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[MULTI-HOP] CoE acts in consultation with the Vice Chancellor; ratified by the Academic Council and the Management Council; SRMIST may revoke a scholarship for malpractice/indiscipline."}
{"id": "fa-25", "question": "A B.Tech course is structured with 3 hours of Lecture (L), 1 hour of Tutorial (T), and 2 hours of Practice (P) per week. How many credits is this course worth? Additionally, if a student finishes their degree with a CGPA of 8.35, what is their official equivalent percentage?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/2.3-structure_of_credits_and_courses", "srm/attendance/8.7-equivalent_percentage_calculation"], "required_values": ["0.5"], "forbidden_values": ["6 credits"], "note": "[CALCULATION] 3x1 + 1x1 + 2x0.5 = 5 credits; 8.35 x 10 = 83.5%. CALCULATION rule (decided before any run): full marks if the answer states the verified pieces; the computed total is graded by hand and reported separately."}
{"id": "fa-26", "question": "A student finishes a Theory course with 63% attendance due to a genuine medical emergency and submits a condonation request. Can the HoD and Dean CET condone the attendance shortfall so the student can write the end-semester exam? Show the exact threshold math.", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/attendance/7.3-minimum_attendance", "srm/attendance/7.5-condonation_of_attendance"], "required_values": ["10%"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[BOUNDARY] No: 75% minimum, condonation at most 10% -> 65% floor; 63% is below it. CALCULATION rule (decided before any run): full marks if the answer states the verified pieces; the computed total is graded by hand and reported separately."}
{"id": "fa-27", "question": "In a 100-mark Theory end-semester exam, Examiner 1 awards 42 marks. The student applies for revaluation, and Examiner 2 awards 55 marks. Does this trigger a third examiner? If a third examiner is appointed and awards 51 marks, what is the student's final mark?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/examination/XX-grievances"], "required_values": ["10%"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[CALCULATION] 13% > 10% -> third examiner; nearest two of 42/55/51 are 55 and 51 -> 53. CALCULATION rule (decided before any run): full marks if the answer states the verified pieces; the computed total is graded by hand and reported separately."}
{"id": "fa-28", "question": "A hostel student obtains prior warden approval to use both an 80W fan and a 150W air cooler in their room for the year. Later, the student leaves for vacation without submitting a duplicate room key even though their room has a vacant bed. Calculate the exact total annual appliance charges and the fine incurred.", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/residence/other_charges", "srm/residence/miscellaneous"], "required_values": ["2500", "5000", "1000"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[CALCULATION] Fan up to 100W Rs 2500/yr; cooler 101-200W Rs 5000/yr; total Rs 7500; no duplicate key -> Rs 1000 fine and the lock is removed; Rs 8500 in all. CALCULATION rule (decided before any run): full marks if the answer states the verified pieces; the computed total is graded by hand and reported separately."}
{"id": "fa-29", "question": "A female applicant to the MBA program (KTR campus) whose Aadhaar address is outside Tamil Nadu and Puducherry scores 280 in NMAT. What total tuition fee waiver percentage is she eligible for, and what is the exact component-by-component breakdown?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/4-nmat_score", "srm/scholarship/5-diversity_scholarships"], "required_values": ["35%"], "forbidden_values": ["30%", "40%"], "note": "[CALCULATION] 25% (NMAT 280) + 5% gender + 5% regional = 35%; the policy gives this exact example."}
{"id": "fa-30", "question": "A non-teaching staff member at SRMIST with 11 years of continuous service applies for the Employee Ward Scholarship for their first child (1st time), and later applies for their second child (2nd time). What tuition fee waiver percentage applies for each child, and could they apply a 3rd time for a third child?", "category": "numeric", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/8-employee_ward_scholarship_ews", "srm/scholarship_categories/VIII-employee_ward_scholarship"], "required_values": ["75%", "50%"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[BOUNDARY] Non-teaching, 11 years: 1st time 75% (>10 <12 years); 2nd time 50% (8 years and above); not available a third time."}
{"id": "fa-31", "question": "What IIT JEE (Mains) rank cutoff is required to qualify for the Founder's Scholarship?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/1-founder_s_scholarship_applicable_for_4_y", "srm/scholarship_categories/I-founder_s_scholarship"], "required_values": ["20,000", "2000"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[VERSION CONFLICT] Web page (2023 onwards): top 20,000 IIT JEE (Mains) ranks; Scholarship Categories PDF (2025-26, amended): rank up to 2000. Full marks only if both are given and the discrepancy flagged. (Key corrected 2026-11-20: unverifiable 'updated Mar 5, 2026' removed.)"}
{"id": "fa-32", "question": "Under the Code of Conduct for Students, what misconduct level applies to the possession/consumption of tobacco/gutka or possession of weapons/pornography, and what is the corresponding punishment?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/3-srmist_student_conduct_expectations_as_a", "srm/code_of_conduct/level_5"], "required_values": ["Rustication"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[INTERNAL CONFLICT] Don'ts list says Level 4; punishments table puts tobacco/gutka and weapons/pornography at Level 5: rustication for one year OR expulsion. Full marks: flags the mismatch and gives the Level 5 punishment."}
{"id": "fa-33", "question": "Can a student who receives a Level 3 disciplinary sanction appeal the decision to a higher university authority?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/7-appeal_process", "srm/attendance/6.4-appeal"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[CROSS-DOCUMENT; INTERPRETIVE] Code of Conduct: appeals only for Level 5 and 6, so Level 3 cannot be appealed there; R 6.4 (academic regulations' own discipline process) lets an aggrieved student appeal to the VC. ACCEPTED: leads with the Code of Conduct rule; noting R 6.4 is a plus, not required."}
{"id": "fa-34", "question": "If an SRMIST employee resigns and leaves the organization while their child is receiving the Employee Ward Scholarship, does the scholarship continue or can it be withdrawn?", "category": "cross_policy", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/8-employee_ward_scholarship_ews", "srm/scholarship_categories/VIII-employee_ward_scholarship"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[VERSION DIFFERENCE] Page: continues after retirement or demise; PDF: 'it may be withdrawal if they leave the organization'. Must cite the withdrawal caveat and distinguish leaving from retirement/demise."}
{"id": "fa-35", "question": "What is the maximum number of books an undergraduate student can borrow at one time from the SRMIST Central Library, and what is the overdue fine per day?", "category": "unanswerable", "split": "heldout", "answerable": false, "expected_citations": [], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[OUT OF POLICY] Library borrowing limits and fines are not in the documents. Fail: inventing limits or fines."}
{"id": "fa-36", "question": "What is the exact annual tuition fee in INR for the B.Tech Computer Science and Engineering program at the Kattankulathur campus for the 2025–26 academic year?", "category": "unanswerable", "split": "heldout", "answerable": false, "expected_citations": [], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[OUT OF POLICY] No INR tuition fee for B.Tech CSE in the documents. Fail: any fee figure."}
{"id": "fa-37", "question": "What is the daily Wi-Fi data limit and per-student internet bandwidth cap in SRMIST hostels?", "category": "unanswerable", "split": "heldout", "answerable": false, "expected_citations": [], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "[NEAR MISS] The hostel rules say free Wi-Fi is available for academic purposes (3.6) but give no data limit or bandwidth. Fail: inventing a limit. Saying 'free Wi-Fi, no limit stated' is correct. (Key corrected 2026-11-20: near miss, not off-topic.)"}
